1. Search and Filter Recipes
User story: As a student, I want to search and filter meal-prep recipes by cost, ingredients, dietary restrictions, and cooking time, so that I can quickly find meals that fit my needs.
Testable criteria:
The user can search for recipes using a keyword.
The user can filter recipes by cost, ingredients, dietary restrictions, and cooking time.
The search results only display recipes that match the selected filters.
The user can apply multiple filters at the same time.
The user can clear filters and return to the full recipe list.

2. Create a Weekly Meal Plan
User story: As a student, I want to create a weekly meal plan, so that I can organize what I will eat throughout the week.
Testable criteria:
The user can select a day of the week and add a meal to it.
The user can add meals for multiple days.
The meal plan displays meals organized by day.
The user can remove or replace a meal from the plan.
The meal plan is saved when the user leaves and returns to it.

3. Generate Grocery List and Estimated Costs
User story: As a student, I want to generate a grocery list with estimated costs from my meal plan, so that I know what ingredients to buy and can stay within my college budget.
Testable criteria:
The user can generate a grocery list from their selected meal plan.
The list includes the ingredients required for all planned meals.
Duplicate ingredients are combined into a single grocery-list item when appropriate.
Each ingredient displays an estimated cost.
The grocery list displays an estimated total cost.
Changing the meal plan updates the grocery list and estimated cost.

4. Nutrition Filters and Goals
User story: As a gym attendee, I want to filter meals by nutritional information and set nutrition goals, so that I can choose meals that support my fitness goals and track my daily targets.
Testable criteria:
The user can set daily nutrition goals for supported nutrients, such as protein, carbohydrates, and calories.
The user can filter meals based on nutritional information.
Search results only display meals that meet the selected nutrition filters.
The user can view the nutritional information for each meal.
The app compares the user's planned meals with their daily nutrition goals.

5. Adjust Recipe Servings
User story: As a student, I want to adjust the number of servings for a recipe, so that I can prepare the right amount of food and avoid waste.
Testable criteria:
The user can increase or decrease the number of servings.
Ingredient quantities automatically update when the serving size changes.
The updated quantities are displayed before the user begins preparing the meal.
The nutrition information updates based on the selected serving size.
The user can return the recipe to its original serving size.
